{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== AC6 VERIFIED MECHANICALLY, not by eye, and one CI trap worth carrying ===\nExtracted the three guard symbols from origin/main and from HEAD by AST span and compared bytes:\n\n    TicketTransport            BYTE-IDENTICAL (5378 bytes)\n    _TransportPortMeta         BYTE-IDENTICAL (3150 bytes)\n    assert_transport_conforms  BYTE-IDENTICAL (1669 bytes)\n\n_backend.py's ONLY change is an appended comment block. No existing test file is touched — the sole\ntest diff is the new guard (+190 lines, 0 deletions). Backend contract / capability / neutrality /\nport-completeness / DC-port / transport-exception suites: 110 passed.\n\n--- CI TRAP: docs/env-vars.md pins LINE NUMBERS, so a pure annotation change breaks a gate ---\nChanges 1222-1225 took Verified-1 on patchset 1. The failing step was the 'Env-var registry drift\ngate' on ALL FOUR matrix jobs (ubuntu py3.11/3.12/3.13 + macos py3.13) — deterministic, not a flake,\nso no 'recheck' would have helped.\n\ndocs/env-vars.md is DERIVED by scanning env-var reads under src/rebar and records each read's\nfile:LINE. Adding import lines to apply_inbound.py, binding_store.py and outbound_differ.py shifted\nthree recorded lines by 2-3, and the committed registry went stale. Nothing about the change is\nenv-var related; the coupling is purely positional.\n\nThe non-obvious part: Gerrit CI verifies EACH change in a stack independently, so regenerating the\nregistry once at the tip is NOT enough — the intermediate patchsets stay red. Fixed by regenerating\ninside the rebase so every commit carries a consistent registry:\n\n    git rebase origin/main --exec 'python scripts/gen_env_registry.py && \\\n      { git diff --quiet -- docs/env-vars.md || \\\n        { git add docs/env-vars.md && git commit --amend --no-edit; }; }'\n\n(--amend --no-edit preserves each Change-Id; verified all four survived.) Then re-ran the gate as an\n--exec over the stack and confirmed GATE-OK on all four patchsets before re-pushing.\n\nAny future change that merely ADDS OR REMOVES LINES above an os.environ read in src/rebar will hit\nthis. Worth knowing before spending a CI round-trip on it."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785702252359544001,"uuid":"629b2035-6af4-40aa-81d9-5d38be882f66"}